<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lebanese Civil War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1975–1990</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lebanese Civil War was fought from 1975 to 1990 among <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a>'s sectarian militias, Palestinian groups and outside powers. Christian, Muslim and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/druze">Druze</a> factions fought over political power, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and Israel invaded and occupied parts of the country. About 120,000 people died, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taif-agreement">Taif Agreement</a> of 1989 ended the war by rebalancing power between the communities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lebanese-civil-war.jpg" alt="Lebanese Civil War" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: James Case from Philadelphia, Mississippi, U.S.A. · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Green_Line,_Beirut_1982.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
